# A flex node's join settings: aks-flex-node/bootstrap.env on its seed volume (seed/make-seed.sh -s,
# hyperv/New-FlexNodeVM.ps1 -Settings). A systemd environment file, not a shell script: no quotes
# needed, `$` and `%` are taken literally; wrap a JSON value in single quotes.
# The variables are those of AKSFlexNode's bootstrap.sh (`bootstrap.sh --help`); the image adds the
# agent it stages and always fetches fresh bootstrap data.

AKS_FLEX_NODE_CLUSTER_RESOURCE_ID=/subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<resource-group>/providers/Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/<cluster>
AKS_FLEX_NODE_AGENT_POOL_NAME=<flex-pool>

# A host outside Azure without Azure Arc: a service principal with the Azure Kubernetes Service Flex
# Node Agent Role on the pool. Its certificate (PEM with the private key, or an unencrypted .pfx)
# goes next to this file on the seed volume and lands in /etc/aks-flex-node/credentials/, mode 0600;
# the agent keeps reading it while the node is attached.
AKS_FLEX_NODE_AUTH=service-principal
AKS_FLEX_NODE_SP_TENANT_ID=<tenant-id>
AKS_FLEX_NODE_SP_CLIENT_ID=<client-id>
AKS_FLEX_NODE_SP_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_FILE=/etc/aks-flex-node/credentials/sp-client-certificate.pem

# Or Azure Arc (Microsoft's recommendation outside Azure): the host connects at its first boot with
# an onboarding service principal (role Azure Connected Machine Onboarding) whose certificate is
# deleted once connected; then give the Arc machine's identity the Flex Node Agent Role on the pool -
# the join retries until it has it. Leave out the ONEK8S_ARC_* lines for a host already connected.
#AKS_FLEX_NODE_AUTH=arc
#ONEK8S_ARC_TENANT_ID=<tenant-id>
#ONEK8S_ARC_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=<subscription-id>
#ONEK8S_ARC_RESOURCE_GROUP=<resource-group-of-the-arc-machines>
#ONEK8S_ARC_LOCATION=germanywestcentral
#ONEK8S_ARC_SP_CLIENT_ID=<onboarding-client-id>
#ONEK8S_ARC_SP_CERTIFICATE_FILE=/etc/aks-flex-node/credentials/arc-onboarding.pem
#ONEK8S_ARC_TAGS=platform/team=platform

# Optional: the address the kubelet reports, on a host with more than one.
#AKS_FLEX_NODE_CONFIG_OVERRIDES='{"node":{"kubelet":{"nodeIP":"10.92.0.10"}}}'
